/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237654 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a361fc99-c6c3-5763-b077-11d54bd19f13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186237221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237715 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d525463c-b43a-5061-b33f-8f38a0b0c0cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237732 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e6595c31-e9b8-5500-bed2-a7809530f6dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5bb24474-02b6-5a79-8993-e3afc25833c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237831 #edb/ref 1074 "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 6+6\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{100}\\cdot \\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{10\\cdot 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{35})≈{80.13}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(1,5,-1)$, $Q(5,1,1)$, and $R(2,5,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4443b852-41a5-5a76-994c-081bd2938800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237832 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨1,5,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨5,1,1⟩,\\,r=⟨2,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/30/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,5,0⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "894928dd-75e2-52ce-a7a7-400cde0a1a19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237837 #edb/ref 1074 "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257140 #edb/ref 1080 "{21}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257140 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257140 #edb/r