] [17592186259739 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259739 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0fe9fd8-6607-5b94-bf55-ff9abd1059dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259739 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/87/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284845 #edb/ref 1080 "{93.32}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "079ab0d0-3cbc-5082-b6ab-365990a42e59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284850 #edb/ref 1080 "{54}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284850 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284850 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0